---
source: crates/products/git-proxy/service/src/admin.rs
expression: report
---

======================================================================
SECRET: this report contains the agent private key
======================================================================

CLIENT

Name:        wt-git-abc123
Fingerprint: SHA256:abc123
Proxy:       git-proxy@proxy.example.com:2222
Providers:
  - github.com
  - gitlab.com

SERVER CHANGE

Updated /etc/wt-git-proxy/authorized_keys (mode 0600). The new entry is:

restrict,command="/usr/local/bin/wt-git-proxy serve --config /etc/wt-git-proxy/config.toml" ssh-ed25519 PUBLICKEY wt-git-abc123

FILES THE COMMAND WRITES ON THE AGENT

~/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/wt-git-abc123/id_ed25519 (mode 0600)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
-----BEGIN OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----
PRIVATE KEY
-----END OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----
----------------------------------------------------------------------

~/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/wt-git-abc123/known_hosts (mode 0600)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
[proxy.example.com]:2222 ssh-ed25519 HOSTKEY
----------------------------------------------------------------------

~/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/wt-git-abc123/config (mode 0600)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Host wt-git-abc123
  HostName proxy.example.com
  Port 2222
  User git-proxy
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/wt-git-abc123/id_ed25519
  IdentitiesOnly yes
  UserKnownHostsFile ~/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/wt-git-abc123/known_hosts
  StrictHostKeyChecking yes
  PasswordAuthentication no
----------------------------------------------------------------------

~/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/gitconfig (mode 0600)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
[url "wt-git-abc123:github.com/"]
  insteadOf = https://github.com/
  insteadOf = git@github.com:
  insteadOf = ssh://git@github.com/
[url "wt-git-abc123:gitlab.com/"]
  insteadOf = https://gitlab.com/
  insteadOf = git@gitlab.com:
  insteadOf = ssh://git@gitlab.com/
----------------------------------------------------------------------

CHANGES TO EXISTING AGENT FILES

~/.ssh/config gets this line if it is not already present:

Include ~/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/*/config

~/.gitconfig gets an include.path pointing to:

$HOME/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/gitconfig

INSTALL ON THE AGENT

Paste this entire command into the agent VM as the user that runs Git:

umask 077; d="$HOME/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/wt-git-abc123"; g="$HOME/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/gitconfig"; install -d "$d"; printf '%s' 'LS0tLS1CRUdJTiBPUEVOU1NIIFBSSVZBVEUgS0VZLS0tLS0KUFJJVkFURSBLRVkKLS0tLS1FTkQgT1BFTlNTSCBQUklWQVRFIEtFWS0tLS0tCg==' | base64 -d > "$d/id_ed25519"; printf '%s' 'W3Byb3h5LmV4YW1wbGUuY29tXToyMjIyIHNzaC1lZDI1NTE5IEhPU1RLRVkK' | base64 -d > "$d/known_hosts"; printf '%s' '' | base64 -d > "$d/config"; printf '%s' '' | base64 -d > "$g"; touch "$HOME/.ssh/config"; chmod 600 "$HOME/.ssh/config"; grep -qxF 'Include ~/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/*/config' "$HOME/.ssh/config" || printf '\nInclude ~/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/*/config\n' >> "$HOME/.ssh/config"; git config --global --get-all include.path 2>/dev/null | grep -qxF "$g" || git config --global --add include.path "$g"

ROLL BACK THE AGENT

This removes all wt-git-proxy configuration for this agent user:

g="$HOME/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/gitconfig"; git config --global --fixed-value --unset-all include.path "$g" 2>/dev/null || :; if [ -f "$HOME/.ssh/config" ]; then sed -i '\|^Include ~/.ssh/wt-git-proxy/\*/config$|d' "$HOME/.ssh/config"; fi; rm -rf -- "$HOME/.ssh/wt-git-proxy"

ROLL BACK THE SERVER

Press R and revoke wt-git-abc123 (SHA256:abc123). Client cleanup alone does not
revoke the key on this proxy.
======================================================================
